ategory term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Will Bangladesh join the Mecca defense alliance?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1e49f12e46a915dece598cacf3f2aec59d928ae8643046f2f7a7e8c78a82dcc0</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:47:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T12:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/will-bangladesh-join-the-mecca-defense-alliance/a-78613944--650fbd31b54b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/will-bangladesh-join-the-mecca-defense-alliance/a-78613944?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">While Bangladesh weighs the risks of signing the Mecca Joint Defense Agreement, experts warn that such a move could complicate relations with neighboring India.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal flood: Death toll tops 1,000 as rescue continues</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0c8ea97d3a430e11fa29c31d8171bc3eb5308fe6fe4f9149a7569cbe3c760361</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:47:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T10:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nepal-flood-death-toll-tops-1-000-as-rescue-continues/a-78589460--34fefae74285.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nepal-flood-death-toll-tops-1-000-as-rescue-continues/a-78589460?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nepalese authorities say 4,000 people remain unaccounted for as rescue teams with search dogs comb through mud, rocks and debris.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Court says India must uphold Pakistan water treaty</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f1af81f2d3c34f3cdec0e8fc0d625ab3a647f7dec2636d166ec3d08b1222ed6</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:47:04Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T14:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/court-says-india-must-uphold-pakistan-water-treaty/a-78579010--da39b4ed2f68.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/court-says-india-must-uphold-pakistan-water-treaty/a-78579010?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">An international tribunal has ordered India to "observe its obligations" under a water-treaty with Pakistan.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>With multilateralism in decline, what's next for the world?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a81d8ffc03856ab4acaad6763dddaa704ba9629e65fec8283543140779df579f</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:47:04Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T11:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/with-multilateralism-in-decline-what-s-next-for-the-world/a-78555977--8df5725f7fb9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/with-multilateralism-in-decline-what-s-next-for-the-world/a-78555977?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The global political architecture is shifting, partly as a result of the actions of US President Donald Trump. As nations search for a new world order, some may gain influence and power, while others have much to lose.</summary><category term="TOP STORIES" /></entry><entry><title>Inside the sea cucumber smuggling boom</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f3d3c09316d40f86da8db05f229a41e1888fdd1e826a3427168f63e03f1bcaa7</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:47:04Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T10:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/inside-the-sea-cucumber-smuggling-boom/a-78005662--0b2701be2732.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/inside-the-sea-cucumber-smuggling-boom/a-78005662?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A quiet multimillion‑dollar black market is exploding across the Indian Ocean, driven by one unlikely animal: the sea cucumber.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal flood: Death toll crosses 900, thousands still missing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3ed0069ed20f892a694a15252ced9e26650bc4261aff98f9108f976a1a4cad94</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:47:04Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T07:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nepal-flood-death-toll-crosses-900-thousands-still-missing/a-78568505--ecc2324a1555.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nepal-flood-death-toll-crosses-900-thousands-still-missing/a-78568505?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Rescue teams are racing to reach stranded people, even as nearly 4,800 remain missing. Meanwhile, mass burials have sparked controversy in Nepal.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea hands jail term to Unification Church leader</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ac95f22d97045de7f8c12ffb83504c760f4fd0c66ab6af7c1cb3846c90fc11db</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:47:04Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T06:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-korea-hands-jail-term-to-unification-church-leader/a-78568345--da57a3df202c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-hands-jail-term-to-unification-church-leader/a-78568345?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Han Hak Ja has been convicted on bribery charges after giving the former first lady several luxury gifts. She has denied any wrongdoing.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India's citizen-led school audits test limits of activism</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bdd8f191e47608801375af4f52dce310c05fe5cc065ffcb9508a72c8b4ebe6a2</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:47:04Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T09:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-s-citizen-led-school-audits-test-limits-of-activism/a-78545789--a961d5089d76.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-s-citizen-led-school-audits-test-limits-of-activism/a-78545789?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The student-led "Cockroach" movement is taking its campaign for accountability to government schools, but the activists' methods are encountering growing resistance from authorities.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea leans toward military conscription for women</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:812167d24af450dd8684a7631a69f8fe2f3d28d086ce24ab62a1e92af8078e04</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:47:04Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T07:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-korea-leans-toward-military-conscription-for-women/a-78547426--a0344d8b90da.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-leans-toward-military-conscription-for-women/a-78547426?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Facing a population decline, fewer potential service members and calls for social equality to be extended to national military service, Korea is inching closer to breaking the taboo on women on the front line.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Tragedy in Nepal: How do flash floods happen?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3a2b4bd5a83981c539edf0d2af4f52ff8ecf0f75154b9e2ddd2c76bef1b0e047</id><updated>2026-09-02T04:47:55Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T14:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tragedy-in-nepal-how-do-flash-floods-happen/a-78526421--33dcb9d81b48.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tragedy-in-nepal-how-do-flash-floods-happen/a-78526421?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">When flash floods sweep through the Himalayas, there is often little time to react. Scientists are working to understand the risks and improve early warning systems.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry></feed>
